    {
        "content": "<p>po-nuvai <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15036#issuecomment-6578709663\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15036\">issue #15036</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>hi i saw this issue and i got and idea wether it is really working or not idk i will tell you if that is ok i will raise the pr , so the idea is in we need to arrange the table orderly in the segment during that time in an active segment if there is an expression it will became a trap and crash it so before we can treat it as a passive segment during the startup. when i saw the module it give a passive segment slot in which wasm code cant reach there, so we can calculate the value in the other passive segment before any active segment writes to a table. A trap now leaves imported tables unchanged, so later in the normal active-segment order, it is copied into the table (like table.init), and then the slot is freed (like elem.drop), Segments that cannot trap (ref.func, ref.null, ref.i31, global.get) keep the current fast path. So normal modules see no change. I have a local prototype (about 60 lines). Both test cases from this issue pass with it. Does this approach sound acceptable?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636889663,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793627036
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>po-nuvai edited a <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15036#issuecomment-6578709663\">comment</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15036\">issue #15036</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>hi i saw this issue and i got and idea wether it is really working or not idk i will tell you if that is ok i will raise the pr , so the idea is in we need to arrange the table orderly in the segment during that time in an active segment if there is an expression it may became a trap and crash it so before we can treat it as a passive segment during the startup. when i saw the module it give a passive segment slot in which wasm code cant reach there, so we can calculate the value in the other passive segment before any active segment writes to a table. A trap now leaves imported tables unchanged, so later in the normal active-segment order, it is copied into the table (like table.init), and then the slot is freed (like elem.drop), Segments that cannot trap (ref.func, ref.null, ref.i31, global.get) keep the current fast path. So normal modules see no change. I have a local prototype (about 60 lines). Both test cases from this issue pass with it. Does this approach sound acceptable?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636890108,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793627129
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>po-nuvai edited a <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15036#issuecomment-6578709663\">comment</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15036\">issue #15036</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hi, I'd like to work on this issue. I have an implementation idea and would appreciate your feedback before opening a PR.</p>\n<p>If an active element segment contains an expression that may trap (currently only <code>struct.new*</code> / <code>array.new*</code>, as identified by <code>ConstOp::may_trap()</code>), my proposal is to handle it like a passive segment during module initialization:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>When reading the module, allocate a hidden passive segment slot that cannot be accessed by WebAssembly code (i.e., don't add it to <code>passive_elem_map</code>).</li>\n<li>Evaluate its values along with the other passive segments, before performing any active segment writes to tables. This ensures that if evaluation traps, imported tables remain unchanged.</li>\n<li>Later, process it in the normal active-segment order, copy its contents into the target table (similar to <code>table.init</code>), and then free the temporary slot (similar to <code>elem.drop</code>).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Segments that cannot trap (<code>ref.func</code>, <code>ref.null</code>, <code>ref.i31</code>, <code>global.get</code>) would retain the existing fast path, so normal modules would be unaffected.</p>\n<p>I have a small local prototype, and the first test case from the issue passes. For the second test case, I suspect the expected trap message might be incorrect: casting an empty slot to <code>(ref i31)</code> produces a <code>\"cast failure\"</code> rather than <code>\"null reference\"</code>. Replacing the cast with a <code>ref.is_null</code> check makes the test pass.</p>\n<p>I haven't run the full test suite yet.</p>\n<p>Does this approach sound reasonable? I'd appreciate your feedback on the design before I proceed with a PR.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636890378,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793627200
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15036#issuecomment-6582312544\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15036\">issue #15036</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks for offering to work on this @po-nuvai! Yeah that sounds pretty reasonable to me and pretty closely matches what the spec already says to do in these situations. I think the cost of having an extra allocation around during instantiation is just something we'll have to live with for GC-using modules and if that's ever a problem we can work on optimizing it at that point. </p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636944965,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793636695
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>po-nuvai <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15036#issuecomment-6597770130\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15036\">issue #15036</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks @alexcrichton for the feedback on #15036! This PR follows the design we discussed there.</p>\n<p>A few notes for review:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>I ran the full <code>wast</code> test suite locally, and everything passes.</li>\n<li>The new test <code>tests/misc_testsuite/gc/issue15036.wast</code> fails on <code>main</code> and passes with this change.</li>\n<li>I updated the existing test <code>cow-order-trapping-elem-expr.wast</code> (added in #14925), as its last line expected the old, buggy behavior.</li>\n<li>In the issue's second test case, the expected trap message didn't match. A <code>ref.cast</code> on an empty slot produces <code>\"cast failure\"</code>, not <code>\"null reference\"</code>, so I used <code>ref.is_null</code> instead.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Happy to make any changes. Thanks!</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637107270,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793690267
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton closed <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15036\">issue #15036</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This test:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"WebAssembly\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">module</span> <span class=\"nv\">$M</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">type</span> <span class=\"nv\">$t</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">result</span> <span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">table</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">export</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"t\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"mi\">2</span> <span class=\"k\">funcref</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">table</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">export</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"a\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"mi\">2</span> <span class=\"err\">anyref</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">export</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"call\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">param</span> <span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">result</span> <span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">call_indirect</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">type</span> <span class=\"nv\">$t</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">local.get</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">export</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"get-a\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">param</span> <span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">result</span> <span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">i</span><span class=\"mi\">31</span><span class=\"err\">.get_s</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">ref.cast</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">ref</span> <span class=\"err\">i</span><span class=\"mi\">31</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">table.get</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">local.get</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">))))))</span>\n<span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">register</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"M\"</span> <span class=\"nv\">$M</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">assert_trap</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">module</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">type</span> <span class=\"nv\">$a</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">array</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">mut</span> <span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">import</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"M\"</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"t\"</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">table</span> <span class=\"mi\">2</span> <span class=\"k\">funcref</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">table</span> <span class=\"nv\">$t2</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span> <span class=\"err\">anyref</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"nv\">$f</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">result</span> <span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">elem</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">table</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"nv\">$f</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">elem</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">table</span> <span class=\"nv\">$t2</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"err\">anyref</span>\n      <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">array.new_default</span> <span class=\"nv\">$a</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mf\">0x7fffffff)</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n  <span class=\"s2\">\"allocation size too large\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">assert_trap</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">invoke</span> <span class=\"nv\">$M</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"call\"</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">))</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"uninitialized element\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>fails with:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cargo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wast</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Error</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">script</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"na\">foo</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wast</span><span class=\"o\">'</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Caused</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">by</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">directive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wast</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">21</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trap</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">got</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Core</span><span class=\"p\">([</span><span class=\"n\">I32</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"p\">)])</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and the same with the trap in a later element of the same segment:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"WebAssembly\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">assert_trap</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">module</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">type</span> <span class=\"nv\">$a</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">array</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">mut</span> <span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">import</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"M\"</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"a\"</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">table</span> <span class=\"mi\">2</span> <span class=\"err\">anyref</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">elem</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">table</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"err\">anyref</span>\n      <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">ref.i</span><span class=\"mi\">31</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n      <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">array.new_default</span> <span class=\"nv\">$a</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mf\">0x7fffffff)</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n  <span class=\"s2\">\"allocation size too large\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">assert_trap</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">invoke</span> <span class=\"nv\">$M</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"get-a\"</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">))</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"null reference\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cargo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wast</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Error</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">script</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"na\">foo</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wast</span><span class=\"o\">'</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Caused</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">by</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">directive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wast</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">19</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trap</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">got</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Core</span><span class=\"p\">([</span><span class=\"n\">I32</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">)])</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The spec's <a href=\"https://webassembly.github.io/spec/core/exec/modules.html#exec-instantiation\">instantiation</a> evaluates the element expressions of every segment before running any active segment's <code>table.init</code>, so a trapping expression should leave imported tables untouched.</p>\n<p>Fixing this in my opinion is going to need to be balanced with implementation complexity. This is a vanishingly niche use case which in theory shouldn't come along with a large implementation burden. Nevertheless I figured it's worth opening here.</p>\n</blockquote>",
